NEW_FLAGS = [
 FLAG + "COUNSEL FLAG — rebalanced, QueryBook-first structure (rev. October 8, 2026 (B)).</b> The application was previously framed around the language subsystem: its title, Field, Background, Summary, Abstract, FIG. 1–8 and claims 1–30 were directed to the LEL, and the QueryBook platform figures had no detailed description and no independent claims. This revision (a) retitles the application to the QueryBook system and rewrites the Field, Background, Summary and Abstract QueryBook-first; (b) adds Part A ({A01}–{A32}), the detailed description of the core platform figures; (c) adds independent and dependent core-platform claims 1–20; (d) renumbers the figures from the core outward (former FIG. 9–30 → FIG. 1–22; former FIG. 1–8 → FIG. 23–30; FIG. 31–55 unchanged), with paragraphs, sections and claims renumbered and every cross-reference updated; (e) moves the platform reference numerals to a 6100–8210 series, resolving their collision with the language and identity numerals, and adds them to the Reference Numerals key; (f) relocates the brief descriptions of FIG. 31–49 from Section IX to the Brief Description of the Drawings; and (g) corrects FIG. 5 by removing a stray “(CLAIM 11)” label, removing overlay boxes that hid the waypoint labels, and replacing the undefined label “(IQR)” with “from Fact Units”. This addresses items (b) and (c) of the consolidation flag below. The substantive content of Parts B–D is unchanged apart from renumbering, short part introductions, and the consolidation of the Section XXIII claims noted below.</div>\n",
 FLAG + "COUNSEL FLAG — core claims 1–20 and the related QueryBook provisionals.</b> The core platform (Fact Unit, UFCS, FQL, Prime Directive, certification, federation, erasure) is also the subject of the prior QueryBook, UFCS and FQL provisional applications listed under Related applications. Claims 1–20 may overlap claims of those applications and may be entitled to their priority. Please confirm the priority claims and any incorporation by reference, and decide whether the core claims are pursued here, in the core family, or both. Expect relevant art in knowledge graphs and provenance models, trust-weighted and probabilistic databases, verification of generated text against a knowledge base, cryptographic erasure (crypto-shredding), content-addressed storage and federated data systems; the claims are framed on the combination recited in claim 1.</div>\n",
 FLAG + "COUNSEL FLAG — Part A reduction-to-practice status.</b> {A32} states which core-platform elements are embodied in the QueryBook software prototype and which are specified designs. Please confirm that characterization against the prototype before filing, and confirm that no specified element reads as performed. Numerical values in FIG. 3, FIG. 18 and FIG. 21 are illustrative.</div>\n",
 FLAG + "COUNSEL FLAG — Section XXIII claims consolidated for proportion.</b> The agent-era claims added earlier in this revision cycle were reduced from 23 to 12 (now claims 97–108) so that the claim set reflects the system as a whole rather than its most recent extension. The omitted dependent subject matter remains disclosed in Section XXIII and may be claimed on conversion: typed record kinds and repeatable re-ingestion; archive bounds and non-execution; recovery of page-description text through character-to-Unicode maps; the certificate-is-not-a-truth-claim presentation; the in-system transaction signer with test-vector self-checks and the value-bearing-network guard; the token-holder licence check; firewall signatures and per-caller anomaly scoring; the loopback client key; treating a purge request as a tripwire; the tool-server interface; and leaving skin regions uncolored absent a record.</div>\n",
]

